1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,500
SemaFrame — a semantic spatial workspace for AI agents.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,500
Agents need more than pixels. They need a world they can inspect.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:17,500
A short-lived local connection starts the handshake. The browser stays in charge.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:24,500
The person sees the client identity, fingerprint and every requested capability.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:33,000
The Agent builds a 3D room, physical objects, a bound data chart and a 2D control in atomic transactions.

6
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:41,500
Live data drives the 2D view. A typed event route drives the 3D animation.

7
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Universal Space Data exposes revision-bound identity, transforms, world bounds, colliders and spatial relations.

8
00:00:49,500 --> 00:01:00,500
The bounded physics preflight detects an unsupported body, previews a deterministic settle, and applies an atomic correction.

9
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:07,500
Collision and physics are explicit attributes—and can be turned off when they are not needed.

10
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:13,500
Every human and Agent change shares deterministic history, undo and replay.

11
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:18,000
SemaFrame. Build spaces agents can understand.
